<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ambrosius Aurelianus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ambrosius Aurelianus was a Romano-British war leader of the 5th century who, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gildas">Gildas</a>, rallied the Britons against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> invaders after the end of Roman rule. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/historia-brittonum">Historia Brittonum</a> made him a rival and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vortigern">Vortigern</a>, and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geoffrey-of-monmouth">Geoffrey of Monmouth</a> he became the uncle of King Arthur. He is one of the few figures of post-Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> named by a near-contemporary source.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ambrosius-aurelianus.jpg" alt="Ambrosius Aurelianus" width="320" height="553" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:History_of_the_Kings_(f.66)_Emrys_Wledig.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
